From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:29:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115: the sleep state entry for the
 ADSP's sensor core

The ADSP of SM6115 runs Qualcomm's sensor core (SEE), which reads the
application processor's sleep state from bit 12 of the SMP2P entry
"sleepstate" (smp2p-sleepstate driver). Give the ADSP's smp2p node that
outbound entry, as the vendor device tree does (bengal.dtsi), and the
node that sets it. The vendor tree's inbound entry "sleepstate_see",
through which the sensor core asks for a wakeup, is left out: no event
here is to wake the system that way.

Signed-off-by: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
index 7f24982f5b..108a9e1085 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115.dtsi
@@ -574,6 +574,17 @@ adsp_smp2p_in: slave-kernel {
 			interrupt-controller;
 			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
 		};
+
+		/* the system's sleep state for the ADSP's sensor core */
+		sleepstate_smp2p_out: sleepstate-out {
+			qcom,entry-name = "sleepstate";
+			#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	smp2p-sleepstate {
+		compatible = "qcom,smp2p-sleepstate";
+		qcom,smem-states = <&sleepstate_smp2p_out 0>;
 	};
 
 	smp2p-cdsp {
